19,31.23784,"","","","","","r","Koshary is a filling pasta, tomato sauce, dried onions, chickpeas, lenses dish, and this restaurant is quite famous beyond Cairo for it and its speedy waiters. Rice with mild seems to be quite famous in combination (after) koshary."],["Al Tahreer Koshary Restaurant","restaurant",30.0448,31.23863,"el-Tahrir Street","","","","","r","Popular koshari chain, serves koshari in various sizes though the small (1.4 kg/3 lb) is a good size portion. You can add hot sauce or a lemon sauce. Eat-in or takeaway."],["Hardees","restaurant",30.04386,31.23633,"","","","","","r","On Midan Tahrir Sq. Delivery 19066. Free Wifi."],["Oldish ( Restaurant & Cafe )","restaurant",30.04333,31.23854,"خلف الجريك كامبس، 20 Mohammed Mahmoud","","","","","r","Tasty Egyptian meals. Besides the Oriental breakfast, they also offer English breakfast. Cozy, romantic, stylish place."],["Le Grillon Restaurant & Garden Cafe","restaurant",30.04717,31.23712,"8 Kasr Al Nile","Daily 10AM - 1AM","","","","r","This is a warm and charming old-school restaurant. Serving traditional plates like mixed grill, fatoush and tahine salad, etc. Serves alcohol (beer) and shisha. Mains are around US$10 and soups & salads are US$3. Old songs are played.…"],["The Greek Club","restaurant",30.04923,31.23982,"221 Mahmoud Bassiouny","Open from 7PM","","","","r","Mostly frequented by liberal and leftist Egyptians rather than Greeks, this is one of the best restaurants in Downtown Cairo. The Greek food offered is limited and the menu often erratic, but the dishes they do have in supply are very…"],["Estoril","restaurant",30.0468,31.2375,"12 Talaat Harb","","","","","r","An old-school restaurant, it's been around since 1962, serving Egyptian food."],["Namaste Indian Restaurant","restaurant",30.0502,31.23239,"1115 Nile Corniche","Daily 1PM-midnight","","","","r","Exotic Indian dining experience."],["Bird Cage","restaurant",30.04252,31.23195,"Semiramis InterContinental Cairo, Corniche El Nil","Daily 1PM&ndash;4PM, 7PM&ndash;late.","","","","r","Reportedly the best Thai food in Cairo."],["Champollion Palace cafes","bar",30.049,31.2377,"","","","","","r","The cafes in the shaded alleys to the east and rear of the wrongly named Champollion Palace provide a lovely shaded respite from the noise of the city."],["Odeon","bar",30.0505,31.2388,"6 Abdel Hamid Said St","24 hours","","","","r","This roof-top open-air hotel bar is also a restaurant, but most visitors prefer just to drink or have shisha. Beer (Stella or Saqqara) is LE15. Very popular among backpackers and foreign students. Open during Ramadan. Nice place to sit…"],["Sherlock Holmes pub","bar",30.0503,31.2325,"1115 Corniche El Nil","","","","","r","Atmospheric British-style pub with warm cosy atmosphere. Local and imported alcohol, moderate prices."],["Egyptian Parliament and Museum","sight",30.04016,31.23672,"128 Qasr el-Ainy","","","","","r","Home to the People's Assembly. There are tours offered and a museum chronicling the Egyptian government. Unclear if the tours and museum are operating since the revolution."],["Ethnological Museum","sight",30.0412,31.23588,"109 Qasr el Aini St","Sat-Thu 9AM-1PM","","","","r","Part of the Geographical Society created by Khedive Ismail in 1895, this rather neglected museum displays more modern Egyptian cultural artifacts, and examples of daily life."],["Corniche","activity",30.04399,31.23136,"","","","","","r","An evening stroll along the Corniche is always a good idea. Take a stroll up to the Qasr el-Nil Bridge, where you can see the lion statues at the foot of the bridge. Qasr el-Nil Bridge is a popular spot for young Egyptian couples to…"],["Scarabee","activity",30.04221,31.23162,"Corniche el-Nil","Departures at 8PM and 10:30PM, cruises last two hours","","","","r","Enjoy a romantic evening cruising the Sofitel owned M/S Scarabee on the Nile. Scarabee offers belly dancing, live music, and international cuisine, grilled meats, and vegetable platters served buffet style."],["Akhenaten Centre of the Arts","sight",30.05891,31.22465,"Eastern end of Sharia 26th of July","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Cairo Tower","sight",30.04583,31.22444,"","open 9AM - midnight","","","","r","A distinctive landmark visible from most of downtown Cairo, the Cairo Tower was completed in 1961 and reaches a height of 187 m. Great day and night views over central Cairo and to the Pyramids from the revolving café and restaurant at…"],["Museum of Islamic Ceramics","sight",30.0552,31.2257,"1 Al Marsafi St","Daily 9:30AM-1:30PM and 5:30PM-10PM","","","","r","The museum is located in the former palace of Prince Amru Ibrahim in Zamalek."],["Gezira Sporting Club","activity",30.054,31.22285,"","","","","","r","Includes four restaurants, swimming, lighted tennis, tennis pros and lessons, table tennis, squash, croquet, playing fields, walking tracks, exercise facilities, equestrian, basketball, children's play areas, saunas, bridge and board games."],["Gezira Golf Club","activity",30.05312,31.22194,"","","","","","r","A large public golf course. Admission for non-members is LE20, tournament fees are LE40."],["Nile Maxim","activity",30.0569,31.2263,"opposite the Marriott","","","","","r","Dinner cruise ship, operated by the Marriott, offers an à la carte menu, along with belly dancing, music, and other entertainment."],["Nile City","restaurant",30.04853,31.22851,"Zamalek","","","","","r","Stationary boat on the Nile includes several international franchises coupled an Egyptian grill and a seafood restaurant. Chilis, Johny Carinos, Fish Market & Studio Misr."],["Deals Restobar Zamalek","restaurant",30.05972,31.22411,"al-Sayyid al-Bakri St","daily 2PM-3AM","","","","r","Purportedly the best burgers in Cairo. Doubles as a pub. Open during Ramadan."],["Abou al-Sid","restaurant",30.05944,31.22425,"around the corner from Diwan","","","","","r","Owned by the conglomerate also responsible for Tabouleh (a rockin' awesome Lebanese restaurant in Garden City), and L'Aubergine, Abou al-Sid features high-end Egyptian cuisine and superb fresh juices. Very atmospheric. Make reservations…"],["Le Pacha","restaurant",30.05199,31.22779,"Saray El Gezirah Street, El-Khalig","Daily 1PM-2AM","","","","r","A complex on a Nile boat with several restaurants and cafes inside the boat. Very tasty food and professional service for an upscale price. Le Tarbouche restaurant which serves hearty traditional Egyptian food. In particular, desserts…"],["Drinkie's","bar",30.05941,31.22378,"155 26th of July St.","","","","","r","A liquor store with a wide variety of spirits. One of the few places to find alcohol in this largely Islamic city."],["Simonds","bar",30.05965,31.2224,"112 Sharia 26th of July","Daily 9AM-midnight","","","","r","A small, long-established and highly popular café frequented by expats and students. Rather intimate, space is at a premium with just a few stools available or stand at the bar. Very good cappuccino. A great selection of sweets,…"],["Sip","bar",30.05629,31.2257,"18 Kamal Khaleel, Omar Al Khayam","Daily 8AM-11PM","","","","r","Specialty coffee with interesting cakes and good (comparing to Egyptian standards) coffee. Also good for working as WiFi is stable and inside area is comfortable."],["Deals","bar",30.0599,31.22402,"2 El Sayed El Bakry St","4PM-2AM","","","","r","Another popular pub haunt. Cable TV, DJ and house music. Pub menu. Open during Ramadan. Stella LE15, main dishes from LE25-60."]]}